# Clarified spec:
# Split a restaurant bill evenly among n people and return the list of amounts each person pays, rounded to cents. Amounts are rounded to cents using banker's rounding (half‑cent ties to nearest even cent). Totals with more than two decimals are rounded to cents using banker's rounding before division. Any rounding remainder is absorbed so each person pays the same rounded amount. If n is not positive, the function returns an empty list. Values exactly halfway between two cents are rounded to the nearest even cent (banker's rounding). Negative totals are accepted and split evenly among the people. Example: split_bill(total=50.55,n=2)->[25.27,25.27]; split_bill(total=-50.0,n=2)->[-25,-25].
